        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "SNPs might not have a causal effect on cancers. They might also be a confounding variable for the development of disease.\n\nSequencing error can already be detected through a combination of short and long reads with transcriptomic based batch effect calibration.\nThe fp and fn error of modern single cell transcriptomic and de novo construction is already low, combined with the fact that sequencing remains expensive;\n\n-> it's very hard to see the potential of this study in the meanwhile other than the fact that yes, it can detect snp against sequencing error by recalling from pretrained data"
        },
